decision_conditions:
Reason : 11 - In the absence of a completed Section 106 planning obligation the proposal fails to meet the objectives of Policy LP62 (Planning Obligations) of the Wandsworth Local Plan 2023. In order to mitigate the policy conflict as identified, a Section 106 planning obligation would be required to include, but not be limited to:  

 

Sustainability: 

Carbon off-setting payment of �19,968; 

Be Seen energy monitoring. 

 

Highway and transport: 

Exclusion from CPZ;  

To secure a construction management plan; 

To secure highways works (under a section 278 agreement);  

TfL contribution of �20,000 towards the CS7 Cyclist and Pedestrian Safety Improvement Works. 

Demonstrate as part of the Parking Design and Management Plan, how an additional seven per cent of dwellings could be provided with one designated disabled persons parking space per dwelling in future upon request as soon as existing provision is insufficient. 

 

Others: 

To enter into a Local Employment and Enterprise Agreement securing Employment and Skills Plan and Local Procurement Plan, with the target number of job, training and apprenticeship places based on the Council�s Planning Obligations SPD  

To secure contribution of (�21,175 of Employment and Enterprise Contribution based on the Council�s Planning Obligations SPD); 

Monitoring fee in accordance with calculation set out in the Planning Obligations SPD.
